{"file":"llm-secure-patterns-1.0.0-v2.zip","bytes":828714,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"llm-secure-patterns","description":"Secure design patterns for Claude Code LLM applications: external content ingestion, endpoint hardening, output validation, system prompt design, and multi-agent action surface control. Maps to OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications 2025 (November 2025). Includes /llm-secure-patterns:report to generate audit-ready SECURITY_POSTURE.md and DEVELOPER_RECOMMENDATIONS.md files.","version":"1.0.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/wildblue-ai/llm-secure-patterns","homepage":"https://github.com/wildblue-ai/llm-secure-patterns","keywords":["security","owasp","llm","ai-safety"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/agent-action-surface/SKILL.md","name":"agent-action-surface","description":"Use when designing or wiring up tool_use, function_calling, MCP servers, multi-agent chains, or calling multiple LLM providers (e.g., Gemini for vision plus Claude for reasoning) in the same pipeline — fire this skill during architecture/planning discussions, not just implementation","headings":["Agent Action Surface Control","What this skill does","OWASP mapping","Tiered mitigation options","A: Low","WRONG: agent has all tools","RIGHT: classification agent only gets read tools","Write agent gets write tools only after human approval","B: Moderate (recommended)","Gemini analyzes image -> output wrapped as untrusted -> Claude processes","C: High","Key concepts","Cross-model indirect injection","MCP server trust","Multi-agent privilege escalation","Further reading: OWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026)","`# SECURITY:` comment instruction","What this skill does NOT cover (additional security layers suggested)"],"name_hint":"智能体 · action · surface"},{"path":"skills/llm-endpoint-hardening/SKILL.md","name":"llm-endpoint-hardening","description":"Use when designing or building a web route (FastAPI, Flask, Express, or similar) that accepts user input and forwards it to any LLM API (Claude, OpenAI, Gemini, or similar) — fire this skill during architecture/planning discussions, not just implementation","headings":["LLM Endpoint Hardening","What this skill does","OWASP mapping","Tiered mitigation options","A: Low","B: Moderate (recommended)","C: High","`# SECURITY:` comment instruction","What this skill does NOT cover (additional security layers suggested)","False solutions warning","Existing codebase handling","Before completing this skill"],"name_hint":"llm · endpoint · hardening"},{"path":"skills/output-validation/SKILL.md","name":"output-validation","description":"Use when designing or implementing code where LLM responses are rendered as HTML or markup in a frontend, written to a database, passed to another service, or used to generate emails or documents — fire this skill during architecture/planning discussions, not just implementation. Not for SQL or shell command construction — those require parameterized queries and argument arrays, not string escaping (see the Scope section in SKILL.md)","headings":["Output Validation and Sanitization","What this skill does","OWASP mapping","Scope — what this skill does NOT cover","Tiered mitigation options","A: Low","B: Moderate (recommended)","Escape BEFORE interpolating into HTML; escape only what you'll render,","not values consumed by code (e.g. id lookups, numeric comparisons).","Scan functions return list[Finding] — structured dicts shaped as","{\"type\": str, \"severity\": \"critical\"|\"warning\", \"match\": str, \"message\": str}.","Fail closed on any critical finding; match on \"type\" (stable ID), not","on message text (message wording can change without notice).","Fail closed on any critical finding:","Or filter by specific type (stable IDs — match on \"type\", not message text):","C: High","`# SECURITY:` comment instruction","What this skill does NOT cover (additional security layers suggested)"],"name_hint":"output · validation"},{"path":"skills/report/SKILL.md","name":"report","description":"Review or audit an existing codebase's security posture against the OWASP LLM Top 10. Reads `# SECURITY:` annotations placed by this plugin and falls back to a best-effort source scan when none are present; writes SECURITY_POSTURE.md and DEVELOPER_RECOMMENDATIONS.md. Use when asked to check, review, audit, scan, or report on the security of LLM/AI integration code.","headings":["/report — LLM Security Posture Report","Purpose","Instructions","Step 1 — Collect annotations","Step 2 — Map to OWASP LLM Top 10 categories","Step 3 — Handle unannotated codebases","Step 4 — Staleness detection","Step 5 — Include risk tradeoffs","Step 6 — Generate SECURITY_POSTURE.md","Step 7 — Always append the detailed findings","surface NOT detected","surface detected but unsecured (a confirmed gap)","could not determine","Step 7b — Append the NOT ADDRESSABLE section at the end of the file","Step 8 — Generate DEVELOPER_RECOMMENDATIONS.md","Step 9 — Prompt user about file disposition"],"name_hint":"报告"},{"path":"skills/secure-external-ingestion/SKILL.md","name":"secure-external-ingestion","description":"Use when designing or implementing code that fetches URLs, scrapes pages, calls external APIs, parses PDFs/HTML from untrusted sources, builds RAG retrieval pipelines, or processes any external content that will enter an LLM context window — fire this skill during architecture/planning discussions, not just implementation","headings":["Secure External Ingestion","What this skill does","OWASP mapping","Tiered mitigation options","A: Low","B: Moderate (recommended)","C: High","`# SECURITY:` comment instruction","What this skill does NOT cover (additional security layers suggested)","False solutions warning","Existing codebase handling","Before completing this skill"],"name_hint":"secure · external · ingestion"},{"path":"skills/system-prompt-design/SKILL.md","name":"system-prompt-design","description":"Use when designing, writing, editing, or reviewing system prompts for any LLM application — fire this skill during architecture/planning discussions (before prompts are drafted), not just during implementation","headings":["System Prompt Design","What this skill does","OWASP mapping","Tiered mitigation options","A: Low","WRONG: credential in prompt","RIGHT: credential in external system","api_key is in environment variables, accessed by the tool implementation","B: Moderate (recommended)","C: High","Recommended tooling","`# SECURITY:` comment instruction","What this skill does NOT cover (additional security layers suggested)","False solutions warning","Existing codebase handling","Before completing this skill"],"name_hint":"system · 提示词 · 设计"}],"commands":[],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["llm-secure-patterns","Why This Exists","What It Does","See It in Action","SECURITY: LLM01/LLM10 (Endpoint Hardening) — token-budget rate limiting, spend","circuit breaker, real-tokenizer input cap (fail-closed), and output-token cap","Confidence: MODERATE — mitigates denial-of-wallet, but in-memory limiter/monitor","are single-process (use Redis in prod) and check/record is not atomic (TOCTOU).","Level: Moderate","Declined: High — no tiered budgets, request prioritization, or injection classifier (skipped per developer).","Applied by: llm-secure-patterns v1.0.0 / LLM Endpoint Hardening","Date applied: 2026-06-03","How It Works","1. You start building something LLM-shaped","2. The relevant skill fires automatically","3. You pick a security level","4. Claude writes the code with annotations","5. `/llm-secure-patterns:report` shows your coverage","Install","Usage pattern","How options are presented","Running unattended","OWASP LLM Top 10 Coverage","The 10 OWASP LLM Risks","Why LLM01 Appears in 4 Skills","What This Is NOT","Related plugins"]},{"path":"tests/adversarial-review/README.md","headings":["Adversarial Review Harness","What it does","Prerequisites","Running it","Smoke-test one skill first (~$0.